**/.classpath
**/.dockerignore
**/.env
**/.git
**/.gitignore
**/.project
**/.settings
**/.toolstarget
**/.vs
**/.vscode
**/*.*proj.user
**/*.dbmdl
**/*.jfm
**/azds.yaml
**/bin
**/charts
# ...but NOT application source that happens to live in a directory called charts/.
# The rule above is the stock template's Helm-chart exclusion; booksy-frontend has real
# Vue chart components at src/shared/components/charts/ and
# src/modules/provider/components/charts/ (imported as '@/shared/components/charts'),
# and stripping them from the build context broke every frontend image build with
#   error TS2307: Cannot find module '@/shared/components/charts'
# even though the files are committed -- the workflow's own `npm run build` step sees
# them, only the Docker build did not.
!**/src/**/charts
!**/src/**/charts/**
**/docker-compose*
**/Dockerfile*
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/obj
**/secrets.dev.yaml
**/values.dev.yaml
**/launchSettings.json
LICENSE
README.md
!**/.gitignore
!.git/HEAD
!.git/config
!.git/packed-refs
!.git/refs/heads/**

# Additional exclusions for faster builds
